---
title: Sequence diagram - forgot and reset password (origin/main, 499c39d)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant W as Web portal<br/>ForgotPassword.jsx, ResetPassword.jsx
    participant RL as Rate limiter<br/>auth-strict, 5 per min per IP
    participant AC as AuthController
    participant RTS as PasswordResetTokenService
    participant PP as PasswordPolicy
    participant AS as AuthService
    participant ES as SmtpEmailService
    participant RT as InMemoryRefreshTokenStore
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>User table

    U->>W: email on /#35;/forgot-password
    W->>RL: POST /api/auth/forgot-password {email}
    alt rate limit exceeded
        RL-->>W: 429
    else within limit
        RL->>AC: ForgotPassword(request)
        alt email missing or invalid
            AC-->>W: 400 "A valid email address is required."
        else valid
            AC->>AS: GetUserByEmailAsync(email)
            AS->>DB: SELECT user (falls back to built-in seed users)
            opt user exists
                alt App:BaseUrl not set
                    AC->>AC: log error, send nothing
                else App:BaseUrl set
                    AC->>RTS: CreateToken(user)
                    RTS-->>AC: JWT: email, purpose = password_reset,<br/>pwd_stamp = SHA-256(password hash)[0..16],<br/>audience = password-reset, 30 min, HS256
                    AC->>ES: SendPasswordResetEmailAsync(email,<br/>App:BaseUrl/#35;/reset-password?token=...)
                    Note over AC,ES: Development only: the link is also written to the log.<br/>Smtp:Host, Username or Password missing = email simulated (logged)
                end
            end
            AC-->>W: 200 same message whether or not the account exists
        end
    end

    U->>W: opens the link, enters a new password (12 to 64 characters, checked in the browser)
    W->>RL: POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, newPassword}
    alt rate limit exceeded
        RL-->>W: 429
    else within limit
        RL->>AC: ResetPassword(request)
        AC->>RTS: ValidateTokenAsync(token)
        RTS->>RTS: check signature, HS256 only, audience, expiry (no clock skew)<br/>read email, purpose and pwd_stamp from the validated principal
        RTS->>DB: SELECT user by email (database only)
        RTS->>RTS: compare pwd_stamp with the stamp of the CURRENT hash (fixed-time)
        alt token missing, bad, expired, wrong audience or purpose,<br/>user not found, or password already changed (token used)
            RTS-->>AC: null
            AC-->>W: 400 {message: "Invalid or expired reset token.", errors: []}
            W-->>U: "This link is invalid or has expired", link to ask again
        else token valid
            RTS-->>AC: user
            AC->>PP: Validate(newPassword, user.Email, user.FullName)
            alt fails the policy (length 12-64, 72 UTF-8 bytes, common password,<br/>based on name, email or service words)
                PP-->>AC: errors[]
                AC-->>W: 400 {message: "Password does not meet the requirements.", errors[...]}
                W-->>U: errors under the password field
            else passes
                AC->>AS: ResetPasswordAsync(user, newPassword)
                AS->>DB: UPDATE PasswordHash (BCrypt, new salt)
                AS->>RT: RevokeAllUserTokensAsync(userId)
                Note over RTS,DB: The hash changed, so this link and every older link now fail the stamp check
                AC-->>W: 200 "Password reset successfully."
                W-->>U: /#35;/login with a "password reset" notice
            end
        end
    end
